# docs/modeling/ — Data Modeling

Modeling comes after PRDs and before implementation (`docs/product-map.md` §4). Model only what an approved PRD defines.

- Output lives in `docs/modeling/`, one file per domain: `NNN-<domain>.md` (mirror the PRD number).
- Produce a concise **DSL** first (entities, fields, types, relationships), then derive the **DER** (Mermaid `erDiagram` preferred).
- Enforce per-school isolation: entities carry `school_id` where applicable; enforce family-level isolation for communication.
- Mark **LGPD-sensitive** fields (health, routine, medications, incidents, message content) and note retention needs.
- Use English `snake_case` identifiers (`students`, `messages`, `boletos`). Portuguese only for approved glossary exceptions (`docs/glossary.md`); ask before adding new ones.
- Use the `data-modeling` skill for the full procedure. Detailed guidance: `docs/guidelines/process/`.
